# Arquitectura hexagonal (ms-vehitrack)

Flujo obligatorio:

```text
Handler → Service → UseCase → Port → Adapter
```

## Capas

- `domain/`: entities + ports. Cero imports de application/infrastructure/presentation.
- `application/`: services + usecases + config. Solo depende de `domain`.
- `infrastructure/`: adapters (GCP, DB, publishers). Implementan ports.
- `presentation/`: handlers, dto, routes, middleware, errors, container, server.
- `cmd/api/`: solo bootstrap.

## Prohibido

- Handler → Port / Repository / cliente GCP / SQL
- Service → Infrastructure
- Domain → cualquier capa externa
- Lógica de negocio en handlers, middleware o adapters
- Wire de `services.New*` / `usecases.New*` fuera de `presentation/container`

## Container

- Cablea ports, usecases, services y handlers.
- No exponer getters de clientes concretos GCP/DB a handlers.
- Postgres, BigQuery y Storage son opcionales; Pub/Sub es requerido para telemetría.

Antes de terminar un cambio: `go test ./...` y respetar `scripts/check_architecture.sh`.
